{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Bring all the tithe</b>, and I will pour out blessing upon you — and it will not be destroyed again." "And the meaning of קובעים — like a pledge (משכון) that creditors seize; they withhold what is due to Me." "<b>Will a man withhold</b> — behold, it is the tithe and the terumah that they give not with a grudging eye." "<b>With a curse</b> — you are worthy of being cursed, and you have not designated it for Me. And now, bring it, and I will open the windows of the heavens and pour out for you — by way of parable, concerning the abundance of blessings." "<b>Until there is no lack</b> — not only sufficiency, but more."], :book :malachi, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Malachi -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/malachi"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:13:20.250558385Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}